
  <sn><md>### Whitesur Theme

![img](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nh-em0n/QDoc/main/Programming/linux/Theme/assets/whitesur_theme_screenshot.png)

- Go to this github [repo](https://github.com/vinceliuice/WhiteSur-gtk-theme)
- read the doc 
- clone the repo
  ```bash
  git clone https://github.com/vinceliuice/WhiteSur-gtk-theme.git --depth=1
  ``` 
  it will clone the repo without `.git`
- Open terminal in WhiteSur-gtk-theme you will this kind of file structure 
  ```bash
  $~/Downloads/WhiteSur-gtk-theme lt
	.
	├── clean-git.sh
	├── COPYING
	├── install.sh
	├── libs
	├── make-release.sh
	├── other
	├── parse-sass.sh
	├── README.md
	├── release
	├── src
	└── tweaks.sh
  ```
- Install by running the .install.sh script
  ```bash
  ./install.sh -t all -s nord -a all -n MacOs --shell -b blank
  ```  
  See all the options in the doc.I install all the theme with nord scheme label as Macos and setting shell bg to blank.
  &gt; **Note :** Must include `-l` for gtk version &gt;= 4.0
- Go to tweaks and change your desire theme for both sell and legacy application.
- Uninstalling
  - `./install.sh -r`
  - Remove all the folder from ~home/.themes folder
- Thank u    </md></sn>
